        "question_type": "single_choice",
        "question_title": "The position of a particle moving along the \\(x\\)-axis is \\(x(t)=t^3-6t^2+9t\\) m, where \\(t\\) is in seconds. What is its average speed during the interval \\(0\\\\le t\\\\le 4\\) s?",
        "question_instruction": "Choose one correct option.",
        "explanation": "The velocity is \\(v=\\\\frac{dx}{dt}=3t^2-12t+9=3(t-1)(t-3)\\). The particle changes direction at \\(t=1\\\\) s and \\(t=3\\\\) s. Its positions are \\(x(0)=0\\\\) m, \\(x(1)=4\\\\) m, \\(x(3)=0\\\\) m, and \\(x(4)=4\\\\) m. Hence, total distance \\(=4+4+4=12\\\\) m. Therefore, average speed \\(=\\\\frac{12}{4}=3\\\\,\\\\text{m s}^{-1}\\).",
        "question_audio": null,
        "time_limit_seconds": 30,
        "points": 10,
